{:edb/db-before-t 1623 :edb/db-after-t 1624 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534936 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:45:00.808Z" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186077588 1078 #edb/ref 17592186077591 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078207 1071 "List the like terms for the expression\n\n$$\nx - 2y + 11y - 6z - 5x.\n$$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078207 1071 "List the like terms for the expression\n$x - 2y + 11y - 6z - 5x$." 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186078207 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n$({\\color{red}x}) + ({\\color{blue}-2y}) + ({\\color{blue}11y}) + (-6z) + ({\\color{red}-5x})$\n\nWe see two pairs of like terms:\n\n- The terms $-2y$ and $11y$ are like terms since they both contain the variable $y$.\n- The terms $x$ and $-5x$ are like terms since they both contain the variable $x$." 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186078207 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows: \n\n$$\n({\\color{red}x}) + ({\\color{blue}-2y}) + ({\\color{blue}11y}) + (-6z) + ({\\color{red}-5x})\n$$\n\nWe see two pairs of like terms:\n\n- The terms $-2y$ and $11y$ are like terms since they both contain the variable $y.$\n\n- The terms $x$ and $-5x$ are like terms since they both contain the variable $x.$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078370 1071 "What are the like terms of the expression $4 + 0.8p - 2.3p - 3.2p + 10$?" 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186078370 1071 "What are the like terms of the expression $4 + 0.8p - 2.3p - 3.2p + 10?$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078370 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(4) + (0.8p) + (-2.3p) + (-3.2p) + (10)\n$$\n\nThere are two groups of like terms:\n\n- $0.8p$, $-2.3p$, and $-3.2p$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $p$.\n- $4$ and $10$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186078370 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(4) + (0.8p) + (-2.3p) + (-3.2p) + (10)\n$$\n\nThere are two groups of like terms:\n\n- $0.8p,$ $-2.3p,$ and $-3.2p$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $p.$\n\n- $4$ and $10$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078372 1071 "List the like terms for the expression\n\n$$\n20 - 6a + 2b - 6c.\n$$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078372 1071 "List the like terms for the expression\n$20 - 6a + 2b - 6c$." 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186078506 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444879 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078506 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444882 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078507 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444881 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078507 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444883 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078572 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444878 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078572 1038 #edb/ref 17592186444880 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186078666 1050 420.0 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079135 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079135 1071 "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $a + 2b + 3 - 10b - 9 - 8a$?" 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079135 1071 "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $a+2b+3-10b-9-8a?$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079135 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(a)+(2b)+(3)+(-10b)+(-9)+(-8a).\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $a$ and $-8a$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $2b$ and $-10b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n- $3$ and $-9$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079416 1061 2728 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079416 1061 669614 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079418 1061 2732 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079418 1061 669623 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079419 1061 2735 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079419 1061 669619 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079522 1061 4889 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079522 1061 669615 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079523 1061 4891 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079523 1061 669618 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079524 1061 4892 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079524 1061 669622 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079609 1064 "Terms in a linear expression are called **like terms** if their variable part is the same. For example, in the linear expression\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}2x}+3y{\\color{blue}-5x}\n$$\n\nthe terms ${\\color{blue}2x}$ and ${\\color{blue}-5x}$ are like terms because both terms contain the same variable $x$.\n\nA linear expression may also contain multiple groups of like terms. For example, in the expression\n\n$$\n2a + \\dfrac{1}{2}b + 3a - 0.4 b - a\n$$\n\nwe have two groups of like terms:\n\n- $2a$, $3a$, and $-a$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $a$.\n- $\\dfrac{1}{2}b$ and $-0.4b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b$.\n\n**Remember:** When a term has a subtraction symbol $(-)$ in front of it, the term is treated as a *negative*." 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186079609 1064 "Terms in a linear expression are called **like terms** if their variable part is the same. For example, in the linear expression\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}2x}+3y{\\color{blue}-5x},\n$$\n\nthe terms ${\\color{blue}2x}$ and ${\\color{blue}-5x}$ are like terms because both terms contain the same variable $x.$\n\nA linear expression may also contain multiple groups of like terms. For example, in the expression\n\n$$\n2a + \\dfrac{1}{2}b + 3a - 0.4 b - a,\n$$\n\nwe have two groups of like terms:\n\n- $2a,$ $3a,$ and $-a$ are like terms because they all contain the variable $a.$\n\n- $\\dfrac{1}{2}b$ and $-0.4b$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $b.$\n\n**Remember:** When a term has a subtraction symbol $(-)$ in front of it, the term is treated as a *negative*." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079628 1064 "In some expressions, there are no like terms. For example, in the expression \n\n$$\na+2b\n$$\n\n there are two terms, $a$ and $2b$. These two terms do not have the same variable part, so they are not like terms." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186079628 1064 "In some expressions, there are no like terms. For example, in the expression $a+2b$ there are two terms, $a$ and $2b$. These two terms do not have the same variable part, so they are not like terms." 13194139534936 17592186045417 false] [17592186444842 1080 "No like terms" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444842 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444842 1083 #uuid "05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444843 1080 "$10$ and $10x$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444843 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444843 1083 #uuid "121c5493-ec8e-5d78-ae0c-e87c7710e2d1" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444844 1080 "5" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444844 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444844 1083 #uuid "133b772f-765b-5463-9238-333375439ba6" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444845 1080 "$2y$ and $y$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444845 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444845 1083 #uuid "18cd95de-1fea-58f8-8ec4-e41863840306" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444846 1080 "1" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444846 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534936 17592186045417 tru