s $3$ and $-5$." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444880 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444873 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444880 1069 "q-21823" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444880 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444880 1071 "The like terms in the expression $-x+2y+z+5y$ are" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444880 1072 #uuid "b065b0a1-2f69-56d2-893c-84bf7f3f3787" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444880 1074 "The like terms are $2y$ and $5y$ because they are both terms of the variable $y.$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444881 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444874 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444881 1069 "q-67068" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444881 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444881 1071 "What are the like terms in the expression $3h-v+7u+3t+5x?$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444881 1072 #uuid "b1195c4e-bdb0-5fa7-bea2-b175640ceb43" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444881 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(3h)+(-v)+(7u)+(3t)+(5x).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444882 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444872 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444882 1069 "q-75670" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444882 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444882 1071 "How many pairs of like terms are in the expression $6p-3+5q-2p-3q+1?$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444882 1072 #uuid "b4754c7a-8749-5793-bafb-b31cee518a08" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444882 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(6p)+(-3)+(5q)+(-2p)+(-3q)+(1)\n$$\n\nThere are three pairs of like terms:\n\n- $6p$ and $-2p$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $p.$\n\n- $5q$ and $-3q$ are like terms because they both contain the variable $q.$\n\n- $-3$ and $1$ are like terms because they both contain no variable." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444883 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444876 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444883 1069 "q-101748" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444883 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444883 1071 "What are the like terms in the expression $8x-9y+10z+8$" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444883 1072 #uuid "d0f76c69-d8c0-5996-bfc8-0e524b6847e9" 13194139534936 17592186045417 true] [17592186444883 1074 "We write the terms of the expression as follows:\n\n$$\n(8x)+(-9y)+(10z)+(8).\n$$\n\nNone of these terms have the same variable part. Consequently, there are no like terms in this expression." 13194139534936 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-05878f37-134d-59b9-8f6b-daa44ae9eca0" 17592186444842 "answer-121c5493-ec8e-5d78-ae0c-e87c7710e2d1" 17592186444843 "answer-133b772f-765b-5463-9238-333375439ba6" 17592186444844 "answer-18cd95de-1fea-58f8-8ec4-e41863840306" 17592186444845 "answer-1a4d5dde-dec3-5bd0-bc98-11f4d40df504" 17592186444846 "answer-1d6fb221-0334-5ada-8a0d-1fcb2eb0fcf8" 17592186444847 "answer-265ee5ad-d055-54c9-ada2-8b5881b5c261" 17592186444848 "answer-3bcd6b3e-b205-5407-97e2-2b3abfd8b6de" 17592186444849 "answer-3e8bceef-d437-5965-b3f7-06f784fdb2cd" 17592186444850 "answer-477bd012-e49d-5536-b808-b0e3819359c7" 17592186444851 "answer-48ec5148-d0ac-5e44-9c3c-ea5a699fe9de" 17592186444852 "answer-5b86a1e1-1879-52ac-9479-2f1729eb4348" 17592186444853 "answer-5baf360d-8b56-5d04-b7a0-1a1d7685f8d3" 17592186444854 "answer-5e91f9b6-ccd1-5956-9d4f-018d30330539" 17592186444855 "answer-6e6043cd-809a-58af-90f6-11f0021288ad" 17592186444856 "answer-7e3f8959-2ae0-56f2-b384-9b1ee309c3ac" 17592186444857 "answer-838d51cc-3d11-524b-8c2e-fc03bc3db6de" 17592186444858 "answer-8dd63d6b-1910-5852-bbf8-